# 🔧 Build Guide

This guide will show the main steps used to assemble the Modular 3D Printer. please check the dimensions with the CAD file and BOM befor assembling.

## 1. Prepare the Parts

Before starting, make sure you have all the required components from the BOM.
https://github.com/dhairyaupadhyay097-lang/Modular-3D-Printer/blob/main/BOM.xlsx

### Tools required

- Screwdrivers
- Pliers
- Wire cutter/stripper
- Cable ties
- Multimeter
- Measuring and calibration tools

## 2. Build the Frame

Start by assembling the bottom parts of the cover and the base first and assemble the upper part as part 2 and keep it aside.
Check the frame diagonals to make sure the structure is properly aligned.

## 3. Assemble the Z-Axis

The Z-axis moves the print bed using Lead screws and stepper motor.
1. Install the Z-axis motor with their motor holder
2. Take up the heatbed, glass, and heatbed holder and join them with the couplers to fix it in the lead screws
3. Aling the smooth rods and lead screw wth the bed holder
4. fix the system with the base only when aligned properly with lead screws and heatbed holder

Move the bed by hand to make sure it travels smoothly for smooth rods, and for motors try a testimonial code.

## 4. Assemble the X-Axis

The X-axis moves the E3D hotend with belt and pulley horizontally.

1. Take the top plate of X axis 
2. Attatch the X axis motor firts and the pulley along with the belt
3. Take the hotend and its part, and prepare it, and keep it aside
4. Fixthe smooth rods
5. Now attatch the Hotend part with the belt an the smooth rods properly, also ensure tension shouldn't be excess otherwise the belt will break.

## 5. Assemble the X-Axis

The Y-axis moves the print head ack and forth 

1. Install the 4 pillars first
2. Assemble the motors with their holders and also put the pulley on the motors at that time 
3. Mount motors on the pillars
4. Now, take the x axis part and belt, attatch them and also fix it around the two respective sides of the pillar, and then align all the parts with the belt.
5. Adjust belt tension.

## 6. For the Hotend and Extruder

Mount the extruder and hotend onto the X-axis carriage.

Connect:

* Extruder motor
* Hotend heater
* Hotend thermistor
* Cooling fan

Make sure the hotend is firmly mounted and the filament path is clear.

## 7. For the Heated Bed

Mount the heated bed onto the Y-axis holder.

Connect the:

* Bed heater
* Bed thermistor

Make sure the bed is stable and does not collide with the frame during movement.

## 8. Install the Electronics

Mount the Arduino Mega and RAMPS 1.4 securely and the pwer supply in the electronics box made in the cover.

Connect:

* X/Y/Z stepper motors
* Extruder motor
* Endstops
* Hotend
* Heated bed
* Thermistors
* Cooling fans
* Power supply

Also try to make a path for the cable along the surfaces like house wiring, dont let them fly inside the priinter, as much as possible

**Do not power the printer until every connection has been checked.**

## 9. Firmware

Install the Marlin firmware provided in the `Firmware/` folder.

Before operating the printer, verify the following:

* Build volume
* Motor directions
* Steps/mm
* Endstops
* Thermistors
* Temperature limits

## 10. Final Checks

Before the first power-on:

* Check all screws and fasteners.
* Check belt tension.
* Move X, Y and Z manually.
* Check all wiring.
* Make sure wires do not touch moving parts.
* Verify the thermistors are connected.
* Make sure the hotend and bed are securely mounted and dont let them cross each other as it would damge themselves.

## 11. First Test

After completing the assembly:

1. Power on the printer.
2. Check temperature readings.
3. Test X, Y and Z movement.
4. Test the endstops.
5. Test the hotend.
6. Test the heated bed.
7. Home the printer.
8. Calibrate the printer.
9. Perform a small first-layer test print.

Once everything works correctly, then BOOOM, you got your stuff ready to build craziest things one can imagine!

